>> title: Luncheon Meat and Egg Noodles
>> category: Noodles
>> tags: instant noodles, luncheon meat, eggs, hong kong, breakfast, quick
>> counters: Cha Chaan Teng
>> aka: chaan daan min, gong jai min, 餐蛋麵, 公仔麵, spam and egg noodles, instant noodles with luncheon meat and egg, luncheon meat noodle soup
>> servings: 1
>> time: 15 min
>> slack: narrow — two minutes, not the four the packet says: these finish in the hot broth in the bowl, and noodles boiled to the packet time collapse into it

>> step: fry the slices 4 min, both sides browned
Fry @tinned luncheon meat{4%slices}(1/4-in thick) in @neutral oil{2%tsp} in a #frying pan{} for ~fry{4%min}, turning once, until both faces have browned and gone slightly crisp at the edge.

>> step: fry the egg 3 min, yolk loose
Fry @egg{1%large} in the same pan for ~fry{3%min}, spooning fat over the white and leaving the yolk loose.

>> step: boil 2 min, no sachet
Boil @instant noodles{1%packet}(85 g; keep the block, the seasoning sachet is not used) in @chicken stock{2%cups}(475 mL) with @light soy sauce{1%tsp} and @white pepper{1/8%tsp} for ~boil{2%min}.

>> step: fill the bowl, meat and egg on top
Tip @&(~1)noodles{} and their broth into a deep bowl, lay @&(~3)luncheon meat{} and @&(~2)fried egg{} across the top, and scatter @scallion{1}(thinly sliced) over.
